  "term": "evaluative ratings",
  "definition": "Evaluative ratings are participants’ judgments about how to assess an event or a person’s behavior after it is observed or remembered. In this study, they referred to ratings such as how inappropriate or severe the professor’s behavior seemed and how harsh a punishment was recommended.",
